 "check_text": "protocol.py: 1 biology problem (1 warning).\n\n1. WARNING ENZYME-BEFORE-DILUENT: An enzyme was added before the water: ligase\n   line 46:  p20.transfer(vol_ligase, tuberack[\"A2\"], mix_tube, new_tip='always')\n   At line 46 the robot put ligase into tube A5 in slot 3. Take tube A5 in slot 3: at that\n   moment it held only 52.8 ul, all of it neat buffer, and the water came afterwards, at\n   line 49, to make the 290.4 ul of water or buffer the reaction is built on. An enzyme is\n   shipped in 50% glycerol and is meant to be the last thing into a reaction, after the\n   water and the buffer have brought the well to the right dilution. Dropped into neat\n   buffer or a dry well it meets many times the salt it should: a restriction enzyme then\n   cuts at the wrong places (star activity) and a polymerase starts on mis-primed template.\n   Affected: tube A5 in slot 3.\n   Fix: Reorder the additions to tube A5 in slot 3: water and buffer first, then the sample,\n   then ligase last. Or make a master mix of water, buffer and enzyme in one tube, mix it,\n   and hand it out.\n   Source: Thermo Fisher: restriction enzyme key considerations (the enzyme is the final\n   component)\n           https://www.thermofisher.com/us/en/home/life-science/cloning/cloning-learning-center/invitrogen-school-of-molecular-biology/molecular-cloning/restriction-enzymes/restriction-enzyme-key-considerations.html\n   Source: Promega: restriction enzyme resource (add the enzyme last; glycerol and star\n   activity)\n           https://www.promega.com/resources/guides/nucleic-acid-analysis/restriction-enzyme-resource/\n   Source: NEB: Q5 High-Fidelity PCR kit manual (add the polymerase last)\n           https://www.neb.com/-/media/nebus/files/manuals/manuale0555.pdf\n   Source: Qiagen: critical factors for successful real-time PCR (order of addition)\n           https://www.gene-quantification.de/qiagen-qpcr-sample-assay-tech-guide-2010.pdf\n   [0014ba1fb27b]\n\nThe Opentrons simulator (8.8.2) passed this protocol with no error: it checks that the robot\ncan make the moves, not what they do to the liquids.",
